<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodoric I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 418–451</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodoric I was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 418 to 451, ruling the federate kingdom that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> had settled in Aquitaine, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> as its capital. He repeatedly tried to expand towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast at Roman expense, but in 451 he joined the Roman general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> and was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains">Battle of the Catalaunian Plains</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodoric-i.jpg" alt="Theodoric I" width="320" height="554" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Felix Castello · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:F%C3%A9lix_Castello,_%22Teodorico,_rey_godo%22,_1635.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
